Game data
---------

The licences above cover program code only. They give no rights to the
game's data. Burntime's graphics, music, sounds and texts belong to Max
Design. Playable game data is not included in the program downloads.
The README screenshots show game artwork and are not covered by the code
licences above.
You make burntime.pack from your own copy of the game and the remaster's
files (ReadMe, section 2).

A program built from the source with a pack embedded (a developer build)
contains that data. Such a build is for your own use; do not pass it on.


Libraries in the program
------------------------

The AROS program is statically linked with the libraries below. Their
licence texts are in LICENSE.third-party, libiconv's in LICENSE.libiconv.

- SDL2 2.32.10 (zlib licence), with yuv2rgb (BSD 3-clause),
  https://www.libsdl.org/
  ABIv1 builds (x86_64 mainline, Raspberry Pi): built from the SDL2 2.32.10
  release with the AROS contrib patch SDL2-2.32.10-aros.diff (contrib
  45327d2c) and this program's patch
  third_party/sdl2/patches/0001-aros-call-gl.library-through-SDL-own-base.diff,
  which changes how SDL2 calls gl.library; scripts/deps.py applies both.
  The patches and the scripts are in the source archive. ABIv11 build: the
  static SDL2 2.32.10 of the AROS ABIv11 SDK, unchanged; the program
  supplies stand-ins for the six gl.library functions it names
  (sdlmini/src/gl_standins.rs) instead of linking libGL.
- SDL2_mixer (zlib licence) with stb_vorbis (MIT or public domain), for Ogg
  Vorbis and WAV: 2.8.2 with the AROS contrib patch in the ABIv1 builds,
  2.8.1 from the AROS ABIv11 SDK in the ABIv11 build.
- GNU libiconv, LGPL (LICENSE.libiconv), which SDL2 uses.
  The ABIv1 builds (x86_64 mainline and Raspberry Pi) contain libiconv 1.19
  with the AROS contrib patch libiconv-1.19-aros.diff. The ABIv11 build
  contains libiconv 1.14 from the AROS ABIv11 SDK, built from the GNU
  release without patches. The source archive of this release holds both
  versions, the patch and the ABIv11 build recipe.
  The complete source of this program and its build scripts are in the
  source archive, so the program can be relinked with a changed libiconv.
- The Rust core and alloc libraries (MIT or Apache 2.0).


